%erg v1
Title: Merge new-ticket and ticket-new into a single skill
Created: 2026-05-12
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-12T08:00Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Two skills create tickets: `new-ticket` (50 lines) and `ticket-new` (67 lines).
Both do the same job — normalize input to %erg v1 and write a ticket file — but
their templates have drifted: ticket-new adds a `Status:` warning and a format-spec
pointer that new-ticket lacks. When one is updated the other is forgotten.

The raid SKILL.md token-economy rule (line 119) mandates `/ticket-new`. Skills and
agents that predate that rule still reference `/new-ticket`. The dual existence
creates confusion for both humans and model-invoked calls.

## Actions

1. Decide which name to keep (ticket-new is the canonical one per raid rules).
2. Merge any unique guidance from new-ticket into ticket-new.
3. Delete the redundant skill directory.
4. Grep all skills for references to the deleted name and update them.

## Test

- `ls skills/ticket-new/SKILL.md` exists, `ls skills/new-ticket/` does not.
- `grep -r 'new-ticket' skills/` returns no hits (except this ticket if still open).

## Exit criteria

1. Single ticket-creation skill remains.
2. All cross-references updated.
3. CI green.
